**How to implement.** The last two harness functions move, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` is left holding only test assertions and formatting (001 §Q AT-2 '`BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` keeps only test assertions (`assertMuellerEqual`, the error formatting) and opens the product modules'; the S10.1 brief 'sumWeights, directionalSensitivity'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) Into `FitUncertainty.fs`, after `differenceWeights`: `sumWeights (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) (names : ParameterName list) : Result<ParameterWeights, MuellerFitError>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:sumWeights`), built without mutation, 1.0 at each named axis and 0.0 elsewhere, the first name not in `scaling.axes` being `Error (UnknownAxisErr name)`; new `type DirectionalSensitivity = | DirectionalSensitivity of double` with `value`, doc one line: how hard the residual pushes back along one direction of parameter space, ‖J·v‖ for a unit v; and `directionalSensitivity (jacobian : ResidualJacobian) (direction : ParameterWeights) : DirectionalSensitivity` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:directionalSensitivity`), today's normalization and row sums on the carrier's array. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes both and is left with five module bindings and no type, each doc one to three lines: `expectOk` (step 335), `describeErrors`, `describeColumnNorms`, `assertMuellerEqual` and `ensembleSeeds` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:describeErrors`, `:describeColumnNorms`, `:assertMuellerEqual`, `:ensembleSeeds`), their bodies unchanged. Its module doc becomes one to three lines: the test-side assertions and formatting the inverse-problem suites share; the machinery they drive is `OpticalConstructor.Optimization`'s `MuellerFitting`, `BenchNoise`, `RecoveryEnsembles` and `FitUncertainty` (spec 0050 S10.1). An `open` nothing in the file reads any more is deleted. (3) `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`: `isotropicAbsorption` answers `ParameterWeights` as `sumWeights scaling [ ParameterName "e11"; ParameterName "e22"; ParameterName "e33" ] |> expectOk`; `anisotropicAbsorption` answers `ParameterWeights`, its array built as today and wrapped where it is born; in `normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it` the three sensitivities are compared and reported through `.value`, every band and message text unchanged. (4) `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`' class doc sentence 'The fit driver, the residual, the scaling, the measurement-error model and the acceptance arithmetic are all shared with `MuellerInverseTests` through `InverseFitHarness`' (`BiaxialInverseTests.fs:94-95`) names the four product modules instead; the rest of that doc keeps its text. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the weights hold the same 1.0 / 0.0 entries and the norm is the same sum. No test is added or removed. `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` is the one class that reaches `sumWeights` and `directionalSensitivity`. After this step `git grep -n -E "^    let |^type " -- Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` lists exactly `expectOk`, `describeErrors`, `describeColumnNorms`, `assertMuellerEqual` and `ensembleSeeds`.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `FitUncertainty.fs` MUST declare `sumWeights` (a `Result` over `ParameterName`s), `DirectionalSensitivity` and `directionalSensitivity`, and `git grep -n -E "^    let |^type " -- Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST list exactly `expectOk`, `describeErrors`, `describeColumnNorms`, `assertMuellerEqual` and `ensembleSeeds`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.
